 one after the final block, which is what this model does (h + Sublayer(LN(h)), then a final LN). Other differences from Vaswani et al.: GELU in place of ReLU, an MLP width of 2 x dModel (theirs is 4 x, 2048 for 512), learned position embeddings (they used sines and cosines, and report learned ones gave nearly identical results), and an output matrix not shared with the word table (they share it). Residual output projections start smaller by 1/sqrt(2 x layers), the GPT-2 report's 1/sqrt(N) with N residual layers.","vaswani2017":"arXiv 1706.03762","radford2019":"Language Models are Unsupervised Multitask Learners (OpenAI report)","nostalgebraist2020":"interpreting GPT: the logit lens (LessWrong blog post, 31 August 2020)"},"seconds":7.97}
